 "notes": "Plan of the SS Rosalie Moller (108.2 x 15 m), upright on sand at 50 m with her bow due north, as she lay at anchor. Depths from the Red Sea Wreck Project, seawolf-safari.de and dive guides: mast head 17 m before the masts fell, superstructure 30 m, bow 39, stern gear 35, rudder and holds 45, seabed 50. Hold and mast positions follow the usual layout of a three-island steamer and are approximate. Guides disagree on which anchor is out. The route: down to the bridge, forward to the bow, aft past the bombed hold 3 to the stern and back up.",
